# Web3Forms access key for the contact form. Get one at https://web3forms.com
# by entering the inbox you want messages delivered to — no account needed.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is correct here and not an oversight. The key has to travel to
# the browser because the form posts straight from there, and it is not a
# secret: it only ever grants permission to send a message to the one inbox it
# is bound to. Web3Forms rate-limits and spam-filters on their side.
#
# Without this set, the form validates and then tells the visitor it is not
# configured rather than silently swallowing what they typed.
NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB3FORMS_KEY=
